description: 'PROOF RUN. v042 recipe, identical except training.state_reset=10000,
  on the patched trainer that actually carries recurrent state across chunks. TRUNCATED
  TO 1 EPOCH: a divergence proof, not a score run.'
hypothesis: 'the patch to the training loop makes training.state_reset capable of
  changing the weights for the first time. Before it, R was a no-op mask on an already-zero
  state, so v047 (sr=4000) and v048 (sr=10000) came out BYTE-IDENTICAL to v042 (sr=2000)
  while their config differed -- two duplicate runs and a three-point sweep that never
  happened. This run exists to prove the fix: an identical recipe at state_reset=10000
  must now diverge from v042, and the divergence must be visible in the weights, not
  only in the eval grid.'
change_vs_parent: training.state_reset 2000 -> 10000, on the PATCHED trainer (state
  now carried across chunks).
